The algorithm G is said to generate from K in the limit with mistake feedback if, for all enumerations of K, there exists n⋆ ∈ N such that for all n ≥ n⋆:
1. if G is element-based, then G_n(H_n, b1:n−1) ∈ K \ S_n;
2. if G is set-based, then G_n(H_n, b1:n−1) ⊆ K \ S_n.

